WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:02.400
Harry: From Yellow No. 5 to BHT,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.760
here are all the most shocking chemicals

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.580
we've found in fast-food
chains in the UK and the US.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.843
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.270
Over the past season and
a half of "Food Wars,"

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.620
we've found some interesting,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.370
dare I say shocking

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:18.640
chemicals in some of the
foods and food processes.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.270
We've created this
compilation of these moments,

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.920
and Joe and I are going
to react to them now.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.810
Sure, we may not be food
scientists, food experts,

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.330
scientists, or really anything,

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.790
but we do have these fancy lab coats,

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.600
which I think gives us some credibility.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.250
I got mine at Party City!

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.725
Fantastic! Let's dive in.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.770
You know, the only difference is that

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.090
our pepperoni contains beef.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:45.365
Also preservatives
beutohydrolatehydrolazinase

00:00:45.365 --> 00:00:47.580
and beautohadalidblahbityblah.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.270
BHA and BHT.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.960
I can't pronounce them.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.630
They're bad.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:55.020
It turns out that BHA and BHT are actually

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.210
subject to restrictions
in the European Union

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.840
and can't be added to
foods such as pepperoni.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.420
This might be because
studies have shown that

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.800
BHA can cause tumors in rats

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.850
and it's therefore reasonably anticipated

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.080
to be a carcinogen in humans.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.580
You have no idea how much we
spent on those dancing rats.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.660
I mean, what doesn't cause
tumors in rats, right?

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.180
I feel like rats are always
getting cancer anyway.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.660
And they don't say the portions.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.970
Are they eating human-size
portions of BHA and BHT?

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.605
Then, yeah, of course
they're getting cancer.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:24.663
Oh, well.

00:01:25.747 --> 00:01:27.497
I'm gonna die doing what I love.

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.600
Eating banned chemicals.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.697
Put it in my obituary!

00:01:32.697 --> 00:01:34.470
We reached out to Domino's
to get some clarity

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.993
on the pepperoni situation.

00:01:35.993 --> 00:01:38.580
We got our info from
their ingredients webpage.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:39.680
However, when we checked with them,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.810
they told us that their
information was incorrect

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.530
and they've updated it since
to say that BHA and BHT

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.680
have now been removed from the pepperoni.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.200
I think this happened at
some point during 2018,

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.178
they couldn't say exactly when, but, Joe,

00:01:51.178 --> 00:01:52.880
it sounds like you're OK after all.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.838
Gotta say, my hair game is
pretty strong in this one.

00:01:54.838 --> 00:01:55.990
I know it has nothing
to do with chemicals,

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.248
but my stuff was just [clicks tongue].

00:01:59.248 --> 00:02:01.210
My hair's locked in on this one, buddy.

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:03.553
I loved BHA and BHT
because this was kind of

00:02:03.553 --> 00:02:05.970
the first episode of "Food
Wars" where we found a chemical

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:08.650
that actually was kind of
banned and very dangerous

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.390
and didn't appear in the UK.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:11.773
I'm gonna be straight up.
The European Union sounds

00:02:11.773 --> 00:02:13.721
kind of like a buzzkill, right?

00:02:13.721 --> 00:02:15.520
Is that what Brexit was all about?

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.210
"We want BHA and BHT in our food.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.230
We're outta here."

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:21.800
And in the US, our doughnut is made up of

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.008
enriched wheat flour,

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:26.560
[fast-forward noise]

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:27.840
and BHT.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.200
Ah, yes! Our old friend BHT,

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:34.011
aka butylated hydroxytoluene?

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.570
It is banned in the European Union.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:39.030
The International Agency
for Research on Cancer

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.910
suggests -- might I say
strongly suggests --

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.440
"there is sufficient evidence"

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.220
that BHT causes tumor
growth in lab animals.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.120
I'll tell you straight up,

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.250
those doughnuts could be
made of dead cancer rats,

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.550
I'd still eat them. They're that good.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:54.440
Who cares what's in these doughnuts?

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.530
Also, according to WebMD,

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:59.501
BHT is also used to treat genital herpes.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:01.945
That's right.

00:03:01.945 --> 00:03:02.778
I want you to think about that

00:03:02.778 --> 00:03:04.740
every time you bite into a Krispy Kreme.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.590
Genital herpes.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.460
And every time you get genital herpes,

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.230
I want you to think of Krispy Kreme.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.210
I want those two things
together in your mind

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.530
for the rest of your life.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.513
You are welcome.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.440
Tricalcium phosphate,

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.200
diammonium phosphate.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.430
That last guy, diammonium phosphate,

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.555
aka DAP.

00:03:28.555 --> 00:03:30.580
Not the sequel to "WAP."

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.190
What does that stand for?

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.800
It is also used as a fertilizer
and as a fire retardant.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:39.550
So, when we have the next
wildfire outbreaks in this state,

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:40.860
'cause it definitely will happen,

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.643
we're gonna start dropping
Krispy Kremes on those wildfires.

00:03:43.643 --> 00:03:45.643
Problem solved!

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.555
One thing we need to note
about the US Taco Bell menu

00:03:52.555 --> 00:03:54.210
is that items like the Baja Blast

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.230
and the Doritos Tacos Locos,

00:03:56.230 --> 00:04:00.520
I think the shells have an
ingredient called Yellow No. 5.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.620
Yellow No. 5 is not in the UK.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:03.990
Of course it's in the US.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:06.014
In the UK, you usually find Yellow 5

00:04:06.014 --> 00:04:07.760
referred to as tartrazine.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.210
It's on a list of six chemicals
which, when added to food,

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.067
must contain the following warning:

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:15.060
"May have an adverse effect on activity

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.710
and attention in children."

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.380
Tartrazine is a fascinating one because

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:21.750
it's in so many places in America

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.390
and basically nowhere here.

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.190
But, honestly, like, in
things like the Baja Blast,

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:27.040
I don't think that's what's
causing the hyperactivity.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.610
I think it's the million
tons of sugar that they add.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.528
As a medical professional,

00:04:31.528 --> 00:04:33.110
you're not going to Taco Bell

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:35.860
because you were concerned
about what's going in your body,

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.235
you're going to Taco Bell 'cause

00:04:38.235 --> 00:04:40.330
you don't care what's going
in or out of your body,

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.190
apparently.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.130
In some cases, it causes itching and hives

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.598
in people who eat it.

00:04:45.598 --> 00:04:48.180
Disgusting. [laughs]

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.480
Itching and hives? Yep! That's fine.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:51.657
I feel most people who eat that food

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:53.457
already had itching
and hive issues anyway,

00:04:53.457 --> 00:04:54.870
so if it's not coming from the Taco Bell,

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.520
it's coming from, I don't know,

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.960
sleeping on unwashed bedsheets.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.680
Hey, I ate it growing up,
and I'm perfectly fine.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.260
I should note that I have
a full head of gray hair

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:04.585
and I just turned 23.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:06.443
What's up?

00:05:06.443 --> 00:05:07.900
There are a few things to watch out for

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:09.190
on the menu at Five Guys.

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:10.590
Yeah, like the hot dogs.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:12.747
For example, the pickles in the US.

00:05:12.747 --> 00:05:14.650
In the US, the pickles
contain a food coloring

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:17.020
called Yellow 5, or tartrazine.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.750
If this is added to foods
in the European Union --

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:21.530
My hair looks stupid in
the Five Guys episode.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:22.872
Why did nobody warn me?

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:27.310
There is one thing to
look out for on the menu.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.200
If you're in the US and you get a salad,

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.210
the croutons contain
azodicarbonamide, or ADA.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:33.960
This is a substance that's
usually used to make

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.100
vinyl foam plastics, which
form things like yoga mats.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.840
It's actually been banned from use in food

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.230
in the UK since the 1990s.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:43.155
So, this is my comment
on the yoga-mat thing.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.300
It's always something.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.700
Even when we're trying to be healthy,

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.180
our salad has yoga-mat plastic
in it. It's ridiculous.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.520
Like, why do our croutons
have plastic in them?

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.180
Just get regular croutons without plastic.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.280
It doesn't make any sense.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.140
Oh, my God, I want Pizza
Hut so bad right now.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.950
I know it's weird to
stick up for a chemical,

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:02.040
but I want to point out
that to my understanding --

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.970
again, I've done no research on this --

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:06.880
it's not like they're making the yoga mats

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.770
and then taking the chemicals
out of the yoga mats.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:10.990
If you imagine the chemical,

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:13.700
like, one truckload goes
to the yoga-mat factory,

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.870
and the other truckload goes to Pizza Hut.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.610
I'm assuming, right?

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.430
Or are they recycling yoga mats?

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:20.930
If they're doing that, then never mind.

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:21.772
That's really gross.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:27.210
The only ingredient in the US Chipotle

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:30.100
that gave me a bit of pause
was something called gypsum.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:33.180
Gypsum's also known as
calcium sulfate hydrate.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:34.222
Right? OK.

00:06:34.222 --> 00:06:36.650
And Chipotle uses that
in their tofu process

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:38.320
when they separate the
chunks from the liquid.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.480
Gypsum is also found in
drywall, chalk, and shampoo.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:42.313
Of course it is.

00:06:42.313 --> 00:06:44.710
Now, does the gypsum stay in the tofu

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:47.588
or is it just used for
the separating purposes?

00:06:47.588 --> 00:06:48.421
I don't care.

00:06:48.421 --> 00:06:50.690
I'm never getting tofu from Chipotle.

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:51.940
Don't worry about gypsum.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:53.780
It's fine.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.105
You know how they have
those billboards for --

00:06:58.006 --> 00:06:58.920
Yeah, yeah yeah yeah!

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:01.003
Like, just this.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:04.600
And then next to it is:
"Gypsum. Don't worry about it.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.875
You're fine." [laughs]

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:12.250
One piece of information you can get

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:13.650
from the UK's FAQ page

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:16.140
is that the plant-based
Great Imitator wrap

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.270
might not actually be as
plant-based as it seems.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:21.200
The baste and the tortilla
wrap used both contain shellac.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.530
Now, shellac is also sometimes
called confectioner's glaze,

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:25.540
and it's a natural polymer that's used to

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:28.200
give things a waxy finish
and to trap in moisture.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.110
Love the shirt I wore
in the Nando's episode.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:31.895
What's your favorite Harry shirt so far?

00:07:31.895 --> 00:07:33.530
Leave a comment below.

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.220
But where does shellac actually come from?

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.750
Well, it's actually secreted
by female lac beetles

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:40.080
onto trees in India and Thailand.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.720
This means it's technically
an animal product,

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:44.010
and although it can be gathered
without harming the beetles,

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:45.590
this is hard to achieve in practice.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:46.630
Not nice.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:47.910
Shellac was one which popped out to me

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:49.230
when I was reading the ingredients list

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.280
just because the usual
context I've heard it in

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.990
is, like, gel nails.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:55.310
So as soon as I kind of
knew that that wasn't that,

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.880
I wanted to do some more research into it.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:57.978
And it turns out it's a beetle thing.

00:07:57.978 --> 00:07:58.811
Who knew?

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.660
However, after combing
through their ingredients list

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:04.720
in the UK and the US,

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.378
we did find one or two
things to look out for.

00:08:06.378 --> 00:08:07.940
For example, caramel color.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.280
It's used in a range of Pret products,

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.350
from the dressing that
they put on their salads

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:13.490
to the caramel syrups, which
they put into their drinks.

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:15.580
Well, in the US, you'll find caramel color

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:17.600
in the salted caramel hot chocolate

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:20.160
and the salted caramel latte,

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.770
which I drink.

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.298
Caramel color is worth
pointing out because

00:08:23.298 --> 00:08:24.465
it's on the state of California's

00:08:24.465 --> 00:08:26.340
Proposition 65 list of chemicals

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:28.350
which are known to the
state to cause cancer

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:29.895
or reproductive toxicity.

00:08:29.895 --> 00:08:31.990
Ooh, reproductive toxicity.

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:34.760
That's fun. Um. [laughs]

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:35.650
See, I was scared,

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:37.280
but the good news is there's only

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:40.288
two types of caramel
color, classes III and IV,

00:08:40.288 --> 00:08:41.300
that contained the chemical

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.740
that's to blame for this, 4-MEL.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:45.537
The bad news is that
class IV caramel color

00:08:45.537 --> 00:08:47.210
does appear on the menu in the UK.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:48.497
While there is some
evidence to suggest that

00:08:48.497 --> 00:08:50.610
the amounts currently in
our food are pretty safe,

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:53.060
the state of California
banning it isn't a great look.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.690
Meanwhile, at a federal level,

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:58.570
the FDA still says that there
is "no reason to believe

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.540
that there are any immediate
or short-term health risks

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:05.203
presented by 4-MEI at the
levels expected in food."

00:09:06.111 --> 00:09:09.170
So, kind of up to you.

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:10.453
Whenever we reach out to someone

00:09:10.453 --> 00:09:11.737
about something like caramel color,

00:09:11.737 --> 00:09:13.550
the answer tends to be along the lines of,

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.670
"Well, you know, at its
current level, it's fine."

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:16.590
Then surely if there's something

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:18.270
which has a dangerous level,

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:19.900
then just get rid of it altogether.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:22.508
It can't make that much of
a difference. Come on, guys.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:27.459
The one other thing worth
pointing out is the difference

00:09:27.459 --> 00:09:29.420
between the wraps used
in the two countries.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:30.878
There's only one wrap used in the UK,

00:09:30.878 --> 00:09:32.761
and it's this one, the kibbled rye wrap.

00:09:32.761 --> 00:09:33.833
Here's the ingredients list.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:37.160
We also have kibbled rye wraps in the US,

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.060
and the ingredients list
is virtually identical,

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:42.330
but we can also get a plain tortilla wrap

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.470
as part of the falafel and red peppers

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:46.510
and Pret's chicken Parm wraps.

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:48.125
The ingredients list for this wrap

00:09:48.125 --> 00:09:50.090
is a little more alarming.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.780
There's three different gums in here,

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:53.410
but it's actually the fumaric acid

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.750
you may want to watch out for.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:57.880
It's an acidity regulator that's
pretty common in tortillas,

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.200
but the European Union says that

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.550
while it's practically nontoxic,

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:05.070
long-term exposure is
probably toxic to your kidneys

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:06.560
due to the results of studies

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.637
carried out on calves and rats.

00:10:09.637 --> 00:10:11.820
Nice nonanswer. Like,
"We're not saying it's not,

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:13.680
but we're also not saying that it is."

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.355
Long-term effect, kidney damage?

00:10:16.355 --> 00:10:17.900
I'm not worried about it.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:20.940
Again, Dr. Joe says, "It's probably fine."

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:22.170
And then, on that billboard,

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:23.814
I have a cigarette in my mouth.

00:10:23.814 --> 00:10:24.730
[producer laughing]

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:29.700
What we can get is a list of allergens.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:31.432
And it has a couple of fun things to note.

00:10:31.432 --> 00:10:34.127
For example, there is a
significant risk of there being

00:10:34.127 --> 00:10:36.840
traces of seafood in
our banoffee concrete.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:38.983
Did he say banana? Banoffee.

00:10:38.983 --> 00:10:40.349
I'd be more worried about that.

00:10:40.349 --> 00:10:41.520
What the hell's a banoffee?

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:43.650
And there are also sulfites
in our chicken bites

00:10:43.650 --> 00:10:45.370
and in the ShackSauce.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.840
We may or may not also have shellfish

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.283
in our 'Shroom burger, ShackBurger,

00:10:50.283 --> 00:10:52.540
Shack Stack, and SmokeShack.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.860
So, there's no potential seafood

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:55.430
in the UK equivalents of these burgers,

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:57.320
so I have no idea why
there might be shellfish

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.840
in ours here in the US. I
couldn't even guess why.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.297
Still not been explained to me why

00:11:01.297 --> 00:11:02.505
there is a significant risk that

00:11:02.505 --> 00:11:03.980
there could be seafood in a milkshake,

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:06.387
because obviously that is not
something that goes together.

00:11:06.387 --> 00:11:09.246
I do not want a shrimpy
milkshake. No, thank you.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.110
While we might not have an
ingredients list for our bread,

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:16.405
we do know that it's
likely to not be perfect.

00:11:16.405 --> 00:11:18.753
For example, an Irish
court recently declared

00:11:18.753 --> 00:11:20.920
that Subway cannot call its loaves bread

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:22.400
due to the high sugar content.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:26.470
Subway uses more than
10% sugar in their flour.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:29.083
How about they can't call
their sandwiches sandwiches?

00:11:29.083 --> 00:11:30.670
'Cause they're too gross.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:33.370
The high-percentage amount
of their food tasting bad

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:36.020
is the reason it cannot
be called sandwiches

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.253
or edible food.

00:11:37.253 --> 00:11:38.760
So, I actually reached out to Subway

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:39.810
about their bread issue,

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:41.320
and we did get a response from them.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:43.025
The official Subway line on this is:

00:11:43.025 --> 00:11:45.050
"Subway's bread is of course bread.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:46.610
We've been baking fresh
bread in our stores

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:47.750
for more than three decades,

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:49.483
and our guests return
each day for sandwiches

00:11:49.483 --> 00:11:51.962
made on bread that smells
as good as it tastes."

00:11:51.962 --> 00:11:53.800
So, they're sticking with their guns.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.900
Ireland disagrees. Whose side are you on?

00:11:58.770 --> 00:12:01.540
It's worth pointing out one
other FAQ from the UK page,

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:03.615
which is that the UK
Nando's have explicitly

00:12:03.615 --> 00:12:06.760
committed to never using
chlorinated chicken from America.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.150
Chlorinated chicken's
been in the headlines

00:12:08.150 --> 00:12:09.583
a lot recently because it's kind of become

00:12:09.583 --> 00:12:11.291
the face of differing food standards

00:12:11.291 --> 00:12:12.710
between the UK and the US.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.650
It refers to the process of
giving slaughtered chickens

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:16.300
a chemical wash before they're packaged

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:17.771
and sent to consumers.

00:12:17.771 --> 00:12:20.163
What do you guys have against
our chlorinated chicken?

00:12:21.001 --> 00:12:22.558
JK. Joking. You're gonna see.

00:12:22.558 --> 00:12:24.850
Oh, there's so many things
against our chlorinated chicken.

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:27.850
This is done to kill harmful
bacteria like salmonella.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:29.680
Even the European Union admits that

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:32.680
it's unlikely to pose any
health risk to consumers.

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:34.705
But campaigners say that it also

00:12:34.705 --> 00:12:37.780
allows farmers to cover up
lower production standards

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.703
throughout the chicken-rearing process.

00:12:39.703 --> 00:12:41.703
The good news is that it's estimated

00:12:41.703 --> 00:12:43.770
only 10% of US chicken

00:12:43.770 --> 00:12:46.020
actually gets treated with chlorine.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:49.260
So it's not a guarantee that
Nando's chicken in the US

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:50.940
will have been through the process.

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:54.070
But it's an interesting
example of the different

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:57.390
food standards in the UK and the US.

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:58.573
I'm perfectly fine with that.

00:12:58.573 --> 00:13:00.218
Right? I'm perfectly fine with that.

00:13:00.218 --> 00:13:01.550
Yeah, clean the raw chicken.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.360
I mean, what would you
rather have, salmonella?

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:05.690
Get outta here. Like, it's fine.

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:07.540
I have never gotten salmonella.

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:10.772
From what I hear, it's
pretty awful. Trust me.

00:13:10.772 --> 00:13:13.121
I am a diarrhea expert,

00:13:13.121 --> 00:13:15.196
and it sounds unbearable.

00:13:15.196 --> 00:13:17.480
Give me a chlorinated dipping sauce

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.505
with those chicken tenders.

00:13:19.505 --> 00:13:20.655
I'm perfectly fine with that.

00:13:20.655 --> 00:13:22.782
I am not fine with risking salmonella.

00:13:22.782 --> 00:13:24.960
It's fine. Quit being a baby.

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:26.157
That's my third billboard.

00:13:26.157 --> 00:13:29.499
[producer laughing]

00:13:31.726 --> 00:13:33.126
[sirens]

00:13:33.126 --> 00:13:34.459
Cops are coming?

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:36.470
You hear that?

00:13:38.109 --> 00:13:40.025
Oh, s---.

00:13:40.025 --> 00:13:41.700
I gotta write as many
prescriptions as I can

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:42.950
before they take it away.

